id: pm-github-l1ot
title: "The daily release regenerates the changelog with a different status filter than release:check, so an open changelog-unreleased item delivered since the last tag fails the release"
description: "On 2026-10-15 the scheduled pm-github release (run 38705391245) failed in Run release checks with 'Changelog is out of date'. The release step 'Generate changelog and release notes' runs npx pm-changelog in replace mode with its default closed-only status filter, then npm run release:check runs changelog:check through scripts/generate-changelog.ts, which retains closed items and non-closed items tagged changelog-unreleased, then passes closed plus the statuses of those retained items. pm-github-wrmt (delivered by PR 122) was still in_progress and had the changelog-unreleased tag, so it appeared only in the check's output and the release aborted after bumping in the runner (nothing was published). The release workflow and the package scripts must generate the changelog through one code path (the repo's changelog:full script), so a release cannot fail on a disagreement between two generators of the same file."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: changelog,changelog-unreleased,release
created_at: "2026-10-15T09:25:36.259Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T08:21:51.882Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "release.yml generates CHANGELOG.md and the release notes through the package's own changelog scripts with the same status filter as changelog:check; a test fails if the two disagree; a release run with an in_progress item tagged changelog-unreleased and delivered since the last tag either succeeds or fails before any bump with a clear reason"
comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T18:19:00.873Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced the release generator split: release.yml uses pm-changelog closed-only output while changelog:check includes tagged pending work. The next run fails before refreshing the protected release PR. Plan: one canonical generator, rebuild from freshly fetched main, refresh or supersede stale PRs, and enforce one release per calendar day with pure decision regressions. Related: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/144 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/issues/33"
  "2026-10-18T18:22:11.207Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral function-only revert proof: keeping the same decision function and tests, restored the old unconditional same-day eligibility and today-only branch selection. node --test test/daily-release-plan.test.ts failed 2/4 assertions: the old PR branch was abandoned and a second same-day release was allowed. Restored implementation: focused release suites passed 13/13 and the linked PM command passed. The release generator now invokes changelog:full, changelog:check and release:notes; lease-protected refresh updates the reused PR title/version to today."
  "2026-10-18T18:32:32.900Z",codex-agent,"Consumer context: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/pull/145 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/154 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/147 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/pull/163 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/150 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/127. Separate attribution fix: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/issues/33. The proof report contains all 8 real imported terminal rows, exact before/main lifecycle fields, explicit completed_at projection limits, historical release placement and momentum. Six baseline entries are under Unreleased; all 8 projected rows render under historical releases when terminal statuses are selected."
  "2026-10-18T18:34:34.710Z",codex-agent,"Verified the installed gh read boundary against the real repository: number/headRefName selects existing release PR 144. Removed an unnecessary baseRefOid query field that this gh version does not expose. The pure decision uses existing PR identity, current main SHA, last release and today; it intentionally rebuilds even if the existing PR is already based on current main. Focused release tests pass 13/13 after this compatibility adjustment."
  "2026-10-18T18:48:05.868Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/149 is open at e544b02a2bd266c9f7f07de28eec272ea11e7676. A fresh --no-local clone passed strict health with required merge drivers in an isolated home. Current-head function-only revert copies fail exactly 2/4 decision tests; positive suites pass 13/13. Independent decision coverage is 22/22 lines and statements, 12/12 branches and 1/1 functions. Full npm/Bun gates and Node 22/26 CI remain in progress; no merge, release dispatch, tag or publish occurred."
  "2026-10-18T18:57:13.394Z",codex-agent,"CI Node 26 measured exact 100/100/100/100 across all 15 authored modules, but 1 of 897 tests failed: the pinned pm-ops attestation auditor interpreted the new Node heredoc body as shell publish paths. Replaced that heredoc with a single-quoted node -e expression; the canonical auditor now recognizes exactly one publish invocation with provenance. No auditor code, dependency pin, threshold or exclusion was changed. This is a package-owned compatibility workaround for the pinned shell model; full gates are restarting."
  "2026-10-18T21:12:31.150Z",codex-agent,"Code-head CI is green at 12601d6d325d6e6ad1264c0729ff70bb18c90feb: Node 22 and 26 passed, each with 897/897 tests and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage over 15 authored modules. CodeQL and Semgrep passed. Full local npm and Bun release checks are still running through workflow acceptance; no local completion is claimed yet. Sourcery is quota-limited, CodeRabbit skipped review, and Greptile reports an ended trial, so reviewer approval remains missing. CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39156572837."
  "2026-10-18T22:03:27.935Z",codex-agent,"Full local npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0 at code head 12601d6d325d6e6ad1264c0729ff70bb18c90feb. Each ran 897/897 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations and measured exact 100/100/100/100 over all 15 authored modules at unchanged thresholds and dependency pins. Typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, duplication, privacy, production audit, pack dry run, changelog check and publication-attestation checks passed. The linked current decision/workflow/auditor suite also passed 21/21. Function-only revert failed the stale-PR and same-day regressions. Final receipt changes contain tracker records and documentation; changelog regeneration and final-head CI follow before handoff. No merge, release dispatch, tag or publication was performed."
  "2026-10-18T22:51:56.035Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: PR149 threads PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6tu6Ys and PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6tu6Y7 remain unresolved. Trace confirms untrusted release-prefix PRs flow to force-push and by-head PR editing. Restrict the pure planner to same-repository PRs authored by the workflow identity with date-shaped branches, carry the selected PR number to editing, and refuse fresh-branch collisions. Add independent filter regressions and function-only revert proofs. Link completed receipts in report and tracker; new review gates remain pending. PR150 has no review threads; its completed source and validation remain unchanged. No review-thread replies or resolutions will be made."
  "2026-10-18T22:53:06.496Z",codex-agent,"Review security regression proof: reverting only the same-repository predicate makes the cross-repository test fail with ERR_ASSERTION; reverting only exact workflow-author equality makes the foreign-author test fail; reverting only the date-branch predicate makes the non-date branch test fail. Each isolated run exits 1, with tests and remaining implementation retained. Correct implementation passes the 27-test decision/workflow/publication suite, including legitimate stale PR reuse, unpadded dates, GitHub lookup failure propagation and existing-ref collision refusal before push or cleanup. Report now links immutable completed local receipts and final-head CI for the prior heads: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/blob/3de8cde015db5979d6c0ebc9a749bbccd5656d7d/.agents/pm/history/pm-github-l1ot.jsonl and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39170908685 . Review-round full gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-18T23:32:50.519Z",codex-agent,"Review code-head CI is green at febd1215f941369be9e2de2e69dcfc0fc84f25be: Node22 and Node26, CodeQL and Semgrep passed within 40 minutes with 60-second polling. Node26 logs confirm 903/903 Node tests, exact 100/100/100/100 over 15 authored modules, and 903 native Bun tests across 41 files. CI receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39174854832 . Both explicit local release checks are still running, so their completion is not claimed. Review threads have not been replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-19T00:15:30.141Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 full local gates completed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0 at code head febd1215f941369be9e2de2e69dcfc0fc84f25be. Each passed 903/903 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, exact 100/100/100/100 over 15 authored modules at unchanged thresholds and pins. Lines/statements 10471/10471; functions 275/275; branches npm 3177/3177 and Bun invocation 3175/3175. Typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, duplication, privacy, production audit, pack dry run, changelog check and publication attestation passed. Focused suite 27/27; each of the three planner safety predicates independently reverted causes its regression to fail. Legitimate stale bot PR reuse, single-day cap, GitHub read failure propagation and ref collision refusal remain covered. docs/daily-release-refresh.md links prior completed receipts and the current review receipt, distinguishing historical pending comments from completion. Code-head CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39174854832 . Receipt-only head CI and independent fresh-clone strict health follow in the PR. No review-thread replies/resolutions or release actions occurred."
  "2026-10-19T06:28:39.809Z",codex-agent,"Post-merge review follow-up for #151 and #149: expand release PR discovery beyond the default page; deterministically keep the newest eligible date branch and close superseded candidates by number; parse workflow YAML in regression tests. Preserve all ownership filters and release gates."
  "2026-10-19T06:31:11.132Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs for #151: removing only --limit 1000 makes the complete decision-step beyond-first-30 regression fail (ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1). Removing only candidate sorting makes the newest-date/order-independence regression fail (exit 1). Reverting only superseded output or only the shell close loop independently makes the eligible-only close-by-number regression fail (exit 1 each). All implementations restored; focused decision/workflow/publication tests pass 30/30, with typecheck, lint, docstrings and duplication checks passing. YAML is loaded from the pinned SDK's bundled parser, with no dependency changes."
  "2026-10-19T06:31:51.611Z",codex-agent,"Starting unchanged-threshold npm run release:check followed sequentially by bun run release:check, each with isolated Git identity. Linked decision suite executed through pm test: 13/13 passed; result storage is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment is the durable receipt. Registry pm-cli is 2026.10.19; the repository pin remains 2026.10.13."
  "2026-10-19T07:23:50.176Z",codex-agent,"Completed follow-up gates at code head a782879c6d65ad5e71883ded2160ca07993e6843: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each exited 0 with 913/913 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips, and exact 100/100/100/100 across all 15 authored modules. Each measured 10535/10535 lines and statements, 277/277 functions, and 3225/3225 branches, with zero skipped coverage. All remaining gate stages passed at unchanged thresholds, source scope, budgets and pins. Native bun test test/daily-release-plan.test.ts also passed 13/13. Four independent behavioral revert proofs are recorded above. PM linked-test result storage remains disabled by existing policy; completed results are recorded here. No new PM CLI/SDK defects found. Preparing the new follow-up PR; exact-head CI evidence will be recorded in its body: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/compare/main...fix/release-pr-selection-followup"
  "2026-10-19T08:13:11.052Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 of #152, thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6t1WSO: make superseded release PR cleanup best-effort, move it after the selected release metadata is merged, and test that individual close failures warn with PR number and error while later candidates and the release continue. Sweep every release workflow step for non-essential operations that can block publication; preserve fail-closed publication, provenance and verification boundaries."
  "2026-10-19T08:21:09.595Z",codex-agent,"Review-round sweep covered all 23 release steps. Additional non-essential blockers fixed: selected branch deletion in normal/resume paths, PR title/body refresh, merge diagnostic-file deletion, and implicit/explicit step-summary writes. These now warn; summaries are separate from required changelog/notes generation. All seven identity/verification/publish/tag/Bun/GitHub-release/final-gate step definitions are structurally identical to d2abfe6; 20 shell scripts pass bash -n. Focused suites pass 36/36 and native Bun decisions 19/19. Revert controls retained all tests: six runtime reverts (close failure handler, metadata edit handler, diagnostic deletion handler, branch deletion handler, resume branch deletion, summary handler) each fail with ERR_ASSERTION and exit 1. Three configuration reverts (cleanup order, generator summary flag, notes-script summary flag) independently fail their contract assertions, exit 1. Each implementation restored. Publication failure remains an executed negative case: an unconfirmed registry exits 1 without continuation."
  "2026-10-19T08:21:51.882Z",codex-agent,"Starting npm run release:check then bun run release:check sequentially for the cleanup correction, each with isolated Git identity. Linked PM decision suite passed 19/19; tracking-disabled policy remains unchanged, so results are recorded in comments. No dependency pins, coverage thresholds, source scope, test time budgets or publication policy changed."
